    "Clinical guidelines involve the use of stress imaging, computed tomography angiography (CTA), and cardiac magnetic resonance (CMR) for patients with acute chest pain and suspected coronary syndromes. The guidelines discuss various studies comparing these diagnostic modalities and their effectiveness in assessing chest pain in low to intermediate-risk patients. Some of the shown trials and studies demonstrate the utility of these imaging techniques in reducing unnecessary admissions and improving patient care by identifying those with significant coronary artery disease accurately.": "genes",
